5. Senior-Level Interview Questions

Q1. Difference between PUT and PATCH?

PUT

Full resource replacement


PATCH

Partial update


Example:

PUT /users/1

Sends all fields.

PATCH /users/1

Sends only modified fields.


---

Q2. What is Idempotency?

An operation that produces the same result no matter how many times it is executed.

Idempotent:

GET
PUT
DELETE

Not necessarily idempotent:

POST


---

Q3. Why should GET not modify data?

Because:

Browsers cache GET

Search engines crawl GET

Refreshing page triggers GET


Data modifications may happen unintentionally.


---

Q4. Difference between 401 and 403?

401 Unauthorized

Who are you?

Authentication missing.

403 Forbidden

I know who you are,
but you don't have permission.


---

Q5. When to use 200 vs 201?

200

Existing resource retrieved.

201

New resource created.


---

Q6. Why is DELETE idempotent?

DELETE /users/1

After first deletion:

User no longer exists.

Additional DELETE calls don't change the final state.


---

Q7. What status code should be returned after successful DELETE?

Preferred:

204 No Content

or

200 OK

with response body.


---

Q8. What is CORS preflight request?

Browser sends:

OPTIONS

request before actual request.

Purpose:

Verify allowed methods

Verify allowed headers



---

Q9. Why use 429 status code?

To indicate:

Rate Limit Exceeded

Common in public APIs.


---

Q10. Explain Safe vs Idempotent Methods.

Method	Safe	Idempotent

GET	Yes	Yes
HEAD	Yes	Yes
OPTIONS	Yes	Yes
PUT	No	Yes
PATCH	No	Usually
DELETE	No	Yes
POST	No	No



